Based on the screenshots and your repro, the highlighter is “eating” the whole chunk from the first `<` (in `vector<<…`) to the next `>` somewhere else in the file because

```js
const TEMPLATE_ARGUMENT_RE = '<[^<>]+>';
```

will happily span new‐lines (because `[^<>]` includes `\n`) and thus gobble up everything until it finds a `>`.  By restricting that class to not include line‐breaks, we prevent it from crossing line boundaries and accidentally capturing your “stream‐in” operator misuse as a template.  

