What this does:

- Before: `<[^<>]+>` would match across newlines, so it could unintentionally consume your `vector<<1,2,3…;` up to some far‐away `>`.
- After: `<[^<>\n]+>` will only match between `<` and `>` on the *same* line, leaving your stream‐operator usages intact and highlightable again.
